      "n": 14,
      "topic": 3,
      "topicName": "Household bill",
      "measure": "M66b/c",
      "what": "over-collection refund + debt rule",
      "kind": "scored",
      "mark": "Partial",
      "value": 1,
      "quote": "The tendency is to kick the can down the road and leave the the bill for others to pay later. I won't do that.",
      "why": "Commits against intergenerational deferral, which is the argument M66c is built on, with no instrument behind it: no debt rule, no supermajority override, no published debt set, and nothing at all on the over-collection refund. Context, same block: \"I know how much pain and financial hardship can be avoided by planning ahead.\"",
      "url": "https://www.karenrothe.ca/",
